  "conclusions": [
    "Combined1 increased received FPS and offscreen drawn FPS in all9 same-size/repeat pairs and lowered capture-to-draw p95 in all9. Ratio-of-median received improvements are4.83%,2.46%,1.69% at512x288,768x448,1024x576.",
    "These compare the combined bundle against baseline within the newer stack. The bundle includes cached fixed-seed noise/sigmas and CUDA-event timing/removal of intermediate synchronization; these trials cannot attribute the gain to an individual subchange.",
    "Capture-to-draw p99 worsened in2 of9 one-GPU pairs. Fixed trial order and WAN variability limit causal certainty even when paired directions agree.",
    "Two active GPUs increased median received throughput by1.815x,1.972x,2.002x versus one active combined worker. Both models remain resident in both cases, so this does not measure the cost of loading/compiling a second worker or a one-GPU physical host.",
    "Two-GPU latency tails vary materially:512 repeat1 fell to46.18 received/41.36 drawn FPS with p95 age781.34ms and p991876.43ms;768 repeat2 fell to27.45/26.31FPS with p95 age606.76ms and p992185.24ms. These are retained valid measurements despite passing the inter-arrival continuity threshold.",
    "New-stack baseline versus earlier original-stack baseline median increases are4.15%,12.38%,8.34%; newer combined versus original baseline are9.18%,15.14%,10.16%. These are sequential stack-bundle observations, not isolated causal Torch-version gains. Package/runtime changes and WAN/time differences remain confounded. The earlier768 continuity failure remains included as valid quantified timing evidence through its explicit assessment.",
    "Rates measure receive and offscreen2D decode/draw using the browser harness, excluding the actual application upscaler/projector and audio capture. They do not establish actual-app FPS, display presentation or600-second stability. Quality equivalence and a promoted default are not established by this audit."
  ],
